        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'RÄƒzboi',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "RÄƒzboi (Romanian for 'War') is a classic, high-energy card game of chance played primarily by children and families in Romania. While globally known as 'War', the Romanian variant features specific point-values for face cards (often treated as 10s) and a unique 'Escalation' rule for ties, where the number of cards laid down during a conflict depends on the rank of the card that triggered the war. It is a game of pure persistence and endurance.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Part of the ancient 'Battle' family of card games that appeared in Europe in the 17th century. The Romanian version, RÄƒzboi, has been a cultural staple in schools and villages for generations.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card French deck; Ace ranks high. The deck is divided evenly among the players. Suits are ignored; only rank matters for battles and wars.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card French deck; Ace ranks high. The deck is divided evenly among the players. Suits are ignored; only rank matters for battles and wars.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal the entire deck equally (26 cards each for 2 players). Cards are kept in a face-down stack; players never look at their own cards.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Standard War: 3 face-down cards during war.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Peace: Lower card wins (Reverse War).',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Draft War: Hand of 3 to choose from.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
